{"nodes": [{"id": "tests_integration_brokers_redis_streams_docker_compose_redis_streams_redis", "label": "Redis service", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/redis-streams/docker-compose.redis-streams.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Redis 7 ships streams in the open-source build; single-node ephemeral instance with --save '' and --appendonly no, so no persistence and no clustering."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_redis_streams_docker_compose_redis_streams_runner", "label": "Redis Streams runner service", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/redis-streams/docker-compose.redis-streams.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "REDIS_URL redis://redis:6379, gated on the redis-cli ping healthcheck."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_redis_streams_docker_compose_redis_streams_stream_node_max_entries", "label": "stream-node-max-entries 10", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/redis-streams/docker-compose.redis-streams.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What makes the MAXLEN ~ scenario deterministic. ~ trims whole macro nodes and never a partial one, and a node is sealed at whichever of stream-node-max-entries (default 100) or stream-node-max-bytes (default 4096) is reached first. The scenario writes 50 entries of roughly 80 bytes - about 4000 total, sitting on the byte threshold - so whether a second node existed to trim decided the result and the assertion flipped between runs with nothing changing. Ten entries per node puts it well clear of the boundary, in the direction the scenario means to test."}], "edges": [{"source": "tests_integration_brokers_redis_streams_docker_compose_redis_streams_runner", "target": "tests_integrat